<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>virt-interact: third-party licences</title>
<style>
  /* Black on white, as the app (SPEC-001). */
  body { background: #fff; color: #000; font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 60em; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; }
  a { color: #0645ad; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; color: #000; padding: 1em; border: 1px solid #000; }
  li { margin: 0.1em 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>virt-interact is MIT licensed (see <code>LICENSE</code>). It contains the
open-source crates listed below, under these licences. The source code of
each crate is available from the linked page on crates.io.</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<h2>Licence texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}
  <li><a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
